d what acompose and umbra are (lore-project-index)\n2. Check comp rules - lore-self-compensation and kai-career (the standing rule against inventing comp numbers - though that's about Kai's own comp, I should be careful about inventing numbers)\n3. WebSearch for outside references on pricing for comparable things\n4. Give price bands\n\nActually, wait. There's a nuance. \"the standing rule against inventing them\" in kai-career refers to comp rules for Kai. But this is about product pricing. Still, I should not invent numbers without evidence. The outward personality demands I WebSearch before making pricing claims.\n\nLet me start by loading skills and understanding the projects.\n\nLet me load the required skills first. I'll batch these loads.\n\nActually, let me think about what's most efficient. I need:\n1. lore-project-index - to understand acompose and umbra\n2. role-prod-director and personalities - required doctrine\n3. kai-career and lore-self-compensation - comp rules\n4. lore-self-household-index - has break-even rate $137/hr which is relevant for pricing floors\n\nThen WebSearch for market comparables.\n\nLet me start loading skills in parallel.",
