                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "# Loaded: kai-career/references/comp-and-equity.md\n\n# Comp and equity\n\n## Do not insert a number Kai did not ask for\n\n**Read this before writing any number, anywhere.** Kai flagged 2026-08-17 that agents keep inserting compensation preferences she does not hold, the recurring shape being min-maxing toward the top figure on this page. $250K is a ceiling on what agents may assume, never a target to steer toward.\n\n- **Never volunteer a number.** Not in a recruiter reply, outreach, intro-call prep, cover note, LinkedIn post, bio, or any \"what Kai is looking for\" text.\n- **Never derive one** from a market rate, level, title, peer comp, or published band. Those describe what a role pays, never what Kai wants.\n- **An older record is not confirmation.** The unverified section below has not been agreed.\n- **Same rule for on-call.** On-call load is **not** a driver of Kai's job changes, stated directly 2026-08-17, and agents keep filing it in anyway. Never attach it to her tenure pattern or to outward text. \"No open-ended on-call\" is a forward-looking want for the next role, a different claim.\n\n`lore-self-compensation` in `coilyco-bridge/lore` is authoritative and holds the audit state. It mounts on the exec role only, so other roles work from this file and must not fill gaps by inference.\n\n## Comp is not load-bearing\n\n- **Kai does not optimize for comp.** No pre-drafted negotiation prep, no framing role-fit around a number, no comp questions ahead of role-shape, team, scope, or lifestyle.\n- **Applying it:** treat a published JD band as accepted-if-published unless Kai flags otherwise. To \"what number are you targeting?\", the Kai-shape reply is \"the posted band is fine, let's talk about the role.\"\n- **Why:** stated 2026-05-18, Finch call prep.\n\n## Comp floor (hard gate, confirmed)\n\n- **The floor is a sector split.** $170K for nonprofit and government, $200K for everyone else. Confirmed by Kai 2026-08-17, replacing the flat $170K floor and the $220K to $250K strongest-range framing. Below the applicable floor is a hard gate on the recruiting board unless Kai makes an explicit exception.\n\n**Retired 2026-08-17:** \"the floor is a gate, not an ask, never presented to a recruiter as a target.\" Kai declined it during the comp audit. The board's 8-of-120 scoring weight is a board mechanic and stays on the board card. Do not re-derive the presentation guidance from that weight.\n\n## Comp anchor (confirmed)\n\n- **Median offer $200K base, $250K at median plus one standard deviation.** Confirmed by Kai 2026-08-17. Above $250K is reach territory needing offer-stage leverage. Salary history lives in `lore-self-compensation`, not here, because this repo is treat-as-public-safe.\n- **$250K is the ceiling on what agents may assume.** Anchoring at \"top of staff band\" or \"$280K+\" off vibes produces bad prep.\n\n## Public source of truth\n\nThe floor is published at <https://www.coilysiren.me/hiring/>, and the recruiting board treats that page plus <https://www.coilysiren.me/resume/> as canonical scoring inputs. Normally the public page is the newer artifact, so reconcile rather than assuming this file is current.\n\n**The page is currently behind this file.** As of 2026-08-17 it still publishes a flat $170K floor and treats five days onsite as a soft pass, both superseded. `coilysiren/website#119` corrects it. Until that lands, this file wins.\n\n## Equity is not load-bearing\n\n- **No equity in interview prep.** Cap-table mechanics, 409A, exercise windows, refresh grants, vesting cliffs are all out of scope.\n- **Applying it:** collapse \"comp / equity\" to \"comp\" in prep docs. Surface equity asks as one-line questions rather than pre-drafted strategy.\n- **Why:** stated 2026-05-06.\n\n\n---\nFile loaded into context."
